  ],
  "text": "Drop Everest into the Mariana Trench and its peak would still be two kilometres underwater. Eleven kilometres down. It takes four hours just to fall that far. At the bottom, a full tonne presses on every square centimetre. Send a foam cup down and it comes back the size of a thimble. More people have walked on the Moon than have been down there. Anything rigid gets crushed. Anything with a pocket of air is worse. And yet there is life down there. Not enduring it. Built for it. The deepest place on Earth is not a dead end. It is just harder to reach than orbit. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
